WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.940
Xian fills this grid with numbers.

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:05.160
He places the numbers from one to five in the five

00:00:05.160 --> 00:00:07.660
squares in the bottom row, in some order.

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:11.020
In the next two rows, each square contains the sum of

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:13.760
the numbers in the three closest squares in the row below.

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:17.220
The arrows indicate how this addition works for the first

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:18.580
square in the second row.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.740
What is the largest possible value of the number in the

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:22.340
top square?

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:24.760
This is a maximising problem.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.840
We will count how often each bottom number contributes.

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:32.550
The centre counts three times, its neighbours twice, and the

00:00:32.550 --> 00:00:33.250
ends once.

00:00:34.090 --> 00:00:37.910
Put five centrally, three and four beside it, and one and

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:38.910
two at the ends.

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:43.040
Larger numbers in more-counted positions give a larger total.

00:00:43.740 --> 00:00:46.060
The middle sums are nine, twelve, eleven.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:48.840
The maximum is thirty-two: answer C.

